        "original_id": "c2b338ef-0d32-553c-99f4-5d60824dbaff",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jack Elam, William Scott Elam, Charles B. Pierce, Tim McIntire, L. Q. Jones\n- Works: Sacred Ground\n- Topics: Western films, television acting, comedy roles, physical appearance\n\nFacts:\n- Jack Elam was the professional name of William Scott Elam, who was born on November 13, 1920, and died on October 20, 2003.\n- Jack Elam was an American film and television actor best known for numerous villain roles in Western films and later for comedy roles that sometimes spoofed his villainous image.\n- Jack Elam's most distinguishing physical feature was his lazy left eye.\n- Sacred Ground is a 1983 western adventure film directed by Charles B. Pierce.\n- Sacred Ground stars Tim McIntire, Jack Elam, and L. Q. Jones.",
